<title>TUNISIA: Japan grants Tunisia a 17.333 bln yen loan.</title>
<headline>Japan grants Tunisia a 17.333 bln yen loan.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan has granted Tunisia a loan of 17.333 billion yen for for infrastructure and development projects, officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The loan was for sewerage of four urban centres, irrigation projects in southern Tunisia, and the building of a barrage at Ziatine.</p>
<p>The agreement was signed on Wednesday in Tunis by Foreign affairs Minister Habib ben Yahia and Japanese envoy Hideki Harashima.</p>
